# Nose to Nose — architecture

Python-only pipeline: scrape nosetonose.info → extract structured JSON → build static HTML. No Node.js, no template engine.

## Three stages

```text
Stage 1  ./scripts/scrape_all.sh              → data/*.json + data/bodies/*.md
Stage 2  python scripts/extract_structured.py → data/structured/*.json
Stage 3  python scripts/build_web.py          → web/
```

## Key paths

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `ntn_scraper/` | Scrapy spiders, cleaners, pipelines |
| `data/` | Raw scrape output (merge by `id` on re-run) |
| `data/structured/` | Courses, venues, people (full overwrite on re-run) |
| `scripts/` | `extract_structured.py`, `build_web.py` |
| `web/` | Generated static site (full regenerate on re-run) |

## Critical gotcha

Two different `people.json` files:

- `data/people.json` — 5 whole team pages → "People & team" on `other-content.html`
- `data/structured/people.json` — individual people → `people.html`, `people/{id}.html`

They are **not merged**.

## Where to edit

| Goal | Edit |
|------|------|
| Raw page content / scrape behaviour | `ntn_scraper/`, `data/*.json`, `data/bodies/*.md` |
| Structured fields (courses, venues, people) | `scripts/extract_structured.py`, `docs/structured-data.schema.json` |
| HTML layout, CSS, Markdown rendering | `scripts/build_web.py` only — do not edit `web/style.css` directly |

